  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) is much weaker at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation improves the RNA signal, which is the most fundamental architectural question before investing in multimodal fusion or more complex encoders. This experiment (config_002) tests whether moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation helps the already-dominant RNA modality, using the same pca_n2000 encoder as config_001 for a clean, single-factor comparison. It is the best use of the next budget slot because the answer directly determines whether to pursue transformer aggregation, better RNA encoders, or multimodal fusion in subsequent experiments—if multiprofile doesn't help RNA, the search space simplifies dramatically; if it does, it justifies further investment in aggregation and fusion design."
}

